Q: TypeScript type definition of a state machine A: <p>Not exactly that simple, but this would work:</p>
<pre class="lang-typescript prettyprint-override"><code>type AllKeysArrayRecord&lt;T extends PropertyKey&gt; = {
  [P in T]: T[]
};
</code></pre>
<p>The downside is that you need to define all keys as a union when you declare your state machine, which might not be what you are looking for. The problem is that TypeScript doesn't know which keys will be present at the point of initialization of an object so you can't infer the keys at the time when you define the type.</p>

Q: Generic delete of child entities before MarkAsDeleted() to avoid foreign key constraint errors in VirtualEntityDeleted A: <pre><code> private void DeleteDependents(object entity)
 {
     if (entity == null)
         return;

     var properties = entity.GetType()
         .GetProperties()
         .ToList();

     foreach (var prop in properties)
     {
         try
         {
             if (prop.PropertyType == typeof(string))
                 continue;

             if (!typeof(System.Collections.IEnumerable)
                 .IsAssignableFrom(prop.PropertyType))
                 continue;

             // avoid triggering lazy loading
             var value = prop.GetValue(entity, null);

             if (value == null)
                 continue;

             var children = ((System.Collections.IEnumerable)value)
                 .Cast&lt;object&gt;()
                 .ToList();

             foreach (var child in children)
             {
                 DeleteDependents(child);

                 var deleteMethod = child.GetType()
                     .GetMethod(&quot;MarkAsDeleted&quot;);

                 deleteMethod?.Invoke(child, null);
             }
         }
         catch (ObjectDisposedException)
         {

             continue;
         }
         catch
         {
             continue;
         }
     }
 }


